From 73f603b52077640792de94562339969203572685 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:09:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bugfix: shift architecture-sized values, not ints, by
 hypercube dimensions [report R. Perry]

The number of vertices, the terminal domain bound, the domain size and
the bipartition bit of hypercube architectures were computed as
`1 << n`, which is undefined for n >= 31 whatever the size of `Anum`,
so that 64-bit builds, in which `archHcubArchLoad()` and
`SCOTCH_archHcub()` accept dimensions up to 62, produced garbage
sizes. The same int shifts sized the multinode arrays of
sub-architecture and decomposition-defined architecture matchings, the
terminal hash table of `kgraphBand()`, the vertex count of
distributed hypercube graphs, and the vertex and terminal numbers of
the `amk_ccc`, `amk_fft2`, `amk_hy`, `gmk_hy` and `gmk_ub2`
generators, which bounded their dimension from below only.

Shift a value of the target type everywhere, make `SCOTCH_archHcub()`
reject non-positive dimensions, as `archHcubArchLoad()` does, and bound
the dimension of each generator so that all of the values it computes
fit in a `SCOTCH_Num`.

Refs: COR-19, PS-API-3, API-10, CLI-24
